I think that the game's really fun, bu there are some flaws. First off, it's really buggy. I mean so buggy that my friend dying costed me around 30 artifacts, and that he shows up as a random sprite I've never seen before. Secondly, is the fact that a lot of the characters cost extra mone. I get that the game is under a fiver, and most of the DLC is not too pricey, but it's just a shame that you have to spend more than the game's price on it's own, for some extra characters. Also the Amazon Character is a bit P2W.
However, I still would recommend this game, down to the fun factor. I've gotten over a dozen hours of fun out of this game, and I don't plan to stop there. I personally picked up the [not]* complete version in the summer sale, giving me most of the content, and therefore a hell of a lot of fun, but I think getting it in a sale is probably the best idea if you're thinking of getting the game.
Here are just some pros and cons if you don't want my opinion:
Pros:
Very fun;
Lots of replayability, and radomised levels make grinding more fun;
Lots of characters to choose from from the get go;
Easy controls;
Great range of enemies and bosses;
Cons:
Buggy;
Difficult to set up private servers;
P2W at times;
Grinding still can be boring;
TL;DR
Buy it in a sale.

